  "dual_discriminant_theorem": {
    "proved": true,
    "theorem": "For the primitive lattice L=V_+ intersect Z^n, restriction of integer linear forms gives L*=P Z^n.  Thus 2p L* is contained in L, while P e_i has exact order 2p.  Together with |L*/L|=2p^(m^2), this gives L*/L=Z/2 plus (Z/p)^(m^2).  The circle sublattice has odd index in L, hence L is even.  Finally ||P e_i||^2=1/2 makes level 2p fail, while 4p z^T Pz=2(p||z||^2+z^T C z) is even, so level(L)=4p.",
